OBSERVATIONS (not findings; no criterion implicated)
  O1. accounts.accountMatches has a substring fallback, so a pattern like "acct3"
      WOULD claim acct3_..._2.csv. The suffix guard therefore bites only for
      patterns that exclude the suffix (exact names, anchored globs). The new test
      deliberately uses the exact-name case; this is design, not a defect.
  O2. The brief says filepath.Match; the implementation uses path.Match. Equivalent
      for a basename with no separator.
